<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  CANDIDATE, not in use. tauri.conf.json points at Entitlements.plist.

  The smallest set a Developer ID build of LU is expected to need: the
  microphone, and no Hardened Runtime exception at all. Apple runs extra
  Gatekeeper checks on programs that disable library validation, and asks for
  only the entitlements an app cannot work without, so this is where the
  release build should end up.

  It has not run in any build. Before tauri.conf.json is switched to it, one
  Hardened Runtime build has to pass these by hand (the Hardened Runtime is
  enforced for an ad hoc signature too, so no certificate is needed for the
  test): the window renders and chat streams, the bundled engine loads a model
  and answers, dictation and a voice session hear the microphone, MLX image
  generation starts, an update installs. When it passes, this content replaces
  Entitlements.plist and this file goes away.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
